{
  "id": "Compound::DB00731 - Gene::6564",
  "verbalization": "Nateglinide is likely to interact with Slc15a1 through a shared molecular pathway involving Slc15a2. The evidence suggests that Nateglinide binds to Slc15a2, which participates in various transporter activities, including proton-dependent peptide transport and proton/oligonucleotide cotransport. These activities are all part of a broader function of Slc15a2, which is ultimately linked to Slc15a1. The integration of these pathways implies that Nateglinide may modulate the activity of Slc15a1 by influencing the function of Slc15a2, potentially through competitive binding or by altering the cellular environment that supports the transporter activity. The consistent binding of Nateglinide to Slc15a2 across multiple paths supports the hypothesis that this interaction is central to the mechanism by which Nateglinide affects Slc15a1.",
